WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  a fire blazes in the tinder dry forests  north of lisbon  emergency services have been battling to  keep control as a brutal heatwave  engulfs the country  we follow a team that spotted a fire  burning up over a ridge and they are  racing to stop it  planes carrying water help from above  but it's over 40 degrees celsius and  getting hotter by the hour  the problem is that as soon as the  firefighters put one blaze out another  pops up it's just too hot  and too windy here to keep it all under  control and there are families and  communities dotted about these hillsides  who are still in great danger  there are thousands of firefighters  deployed across the country  still not enough to go around for  anxious residents  we opened the gate and we saw everything  burning and i used a tractor to  extinguish the flames feliciano liberal  tells me i'm sad what can we do it's the  third time this has happened  people are being told to evacuate major  roads closed and events cancelled the  warning it will get worse  there's an extensive area that's already  burned says fire commander manuel santos  the risk is varying day by day we are  worried and working to try and minimize  the pain of the people  in the nearby town of fatima an  important place of pilgrimage for many  christians people seek sanctuary from  the sun  this plaza would normally be packed  this extraordinary heat isn't just  limited to portugal of course spain and  france are suffering too and it's  actually expected to get even hotter in  the coming days eventually impacting the  uk later this week and if it feels  anything like this for many people it  will simply be too hot to be outside  it's all being made worse by climate  change which scientists say is driving  increasingly frequent and severe weather  events including heat waves and drought  for the people of portugal and beyond a  new and dangerous reality  hannah thomas peter sky news in portugal

